pproach. No failed services, damaged package state, or executor-created temporary-file residue was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fd172ed31a3a4367","cmd-48cc3ac95b784729","cmd-4d698b4592174099","cmd-aa6726b4a4ec4198","cmd-253d0f6e41a94815","cmd-2a02bbeccd124bf6","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied with direct end-to-end evidence, including persistence through independent node restarts. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity corroborated by fixed lifecycle observations, and recovered DNS behavior were captured.","limitations":["The fixed after-executor listening-socket observation for node1 was empty despite direct executor commands showing dnsmasq listening on 10.100.52.10:53 before and after reboot. The direct service, socket, and query evidence is coherent, but this supplemental observation is unexplained.","The lifecycle collector inventories only bounded generic state and does not independently probe the task-specific DNS answer or resolver configuration."]}
